@startuml
title MVP Resource Instance lifecycle (CREATE / REUSE only)
hide empty description
state "Planned\nPLANNED" as Planned
state "Provisioning\nPROVISIONING" as Provisioning
state "Ready\nREADY" as Ready
state "Failed\nFAILED" as Failed
state "Retired\nRETIRED" as Retired
[*] --> Planned : C5 reserve identity/state path/OWNER binding\nbefore provider call
Planned --> Provisioning : C5 CREATE / reset recovery_verified=false
Provisioning --> Ready : provider success / checkpoint identity+fingerprints+version
Provisioning --> Failed : provider error / preserve actual state
Ready --> Ready : compatible REUSE / inspect actual provider state
Ready --> Failed : missing/drifted provider object / recovery required
Ready --> Ready : C6 collect non-sensitive outputs from durable state
Failed --> Ready : C12 verified owned provider object / audit
Provisioning --> Ready : C12 interrupted apply verified complete / audit
Planned --> Ready : C12 orphan provider object imported and verified / audit
Failed --> Planned : C12 verified absence / SAME identity, recovery_verified=true
Provisioning --> Planned : C12 verified absence / SAME identity, recovery_verified=true
Planned --> Planned : C12 verified absence / recovery_verified=true
Ready --> Retired : explicit final demo teardown / retire active bindings
Planned --> Retired : explicit teardown after verified absence
Failed --> Retired : explicit teardown after verified cleanup
Retired --> [*]
note right of Planned
  Lookup always returns the exact active binding at ALL statuses.
  Existing PLANNED can be selected for a new CREATE only after
  recovery_verified=true; no implicit replacement or UPDATE.
end note
note right of Retired
  Teardown is an operator action outside Developer deployment flow.
  Retired instance has no active OWNER binding; history remains.
end note
@enduml
